# Data safety

User data is sacred — on-device Drift data and, when sync exists, server rows. No change may lose, silently delete, or corrupt it.

## Migrations (Drift and Django)

- Always **preserve existing data**: no dropping, truncating, or rewriting user tables without a copy-forward path. Prefer additive columns/tables.
- Every schema change ships an upgrade path from the **latest released version**; renames/moves copy data, never recreate empty.
- When existing data is at risk, add a migration test: open a DB at the old version, migrate, assert the data survived.

## Import / restore

- Validate the whole file **before** writing anything; reject invalid input with a clear message.
- Writes are atomic (single transaction) — never leave a half-imported state.
- Export must round-trip: anything the app exports, the same or newer version imports back.
- Changing the backup format is breaking → major bump (shared release rule).

## Destructive actions

- User-facing delete/overwrite flows state the consequence and confirm first.
- Prefer soft delete (archive/status flag) over hard delete when the product allows recovery.
- Agents never run data-wiping commands (drop DB, delete app storage, `flush`) against user data without an explicit user order.
